.TH VULN1 1 "2026-04-27" "CECS 378" "CECS 378 Buffer Overflow Lab"
.SH NAME
vuln1 \- Phase Phi target; deliberately vulnerable program (see phase-phi(7))
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vuln1
.B <
.I PAYLOAD
.br
.B vuln1
.B \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B vuln1
.B \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
If you have not read
.BR mainframe (7),
do so first. The attack approach is in
.BR phase-phi (7).

.B vuln1
is the warmup target. At startup it prints two lines to standard output:
.RS
.nf
[buffer @ 0x\fIADDR\fP, size N, pad K]
[saved-eip @ 0x\fIADDR\fP]
.fi
.RE
The first is the runtime address of its fixed-size stack buffer; the
second is the runtime address of the saved-EIP slot in this stack frame
(the slot a stack overflow must overwrite to redirect control flow).
.B vuln1
then flushes stdout, reads up to roughly 8 KiB from standard input in
one
.BR read (2)
call, and copies it into the buffer using
.BR strcpy (3)
without bounds checking. Because both addresses are leaked
.I before
the copy, the same process can both observe and use them even under
Address Space Layout Randomization
.RB ( ASLR ),
and the distance from the buffer to the saved-EIP slot does not have to
be guessed from compiler-dependent layout.

It was compiled with stack canaries disabled, position-independent
code disabled, and an executable stack:

.RS
.nf
gcc -m32 -fno-stack-protector -no-pie -z execstack
.fi
.RE

It is installed setuid to user
.BR oracle (8),
who reads
.IR /srv/flag1.txt .

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary to standard output and exit 0.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version to standard output and exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 2
Misuse (unrecognized argument).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /srv/flag1.txt
The flag file readable only by user
.BR oracle .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phase-phi (7),
.BR mainframe (7),
.BR vuln2 (1),
.BR oracle (8),
.BR strcpy (3),
.BR execstack (8)
.SH BUGS
The program is the bug. That is the point.
.SH HISTORY
Written in 1996 and has not had a CVE filed against it because it does
not need one. It is the bug.
